# Canonical domain is https://www.shs-enterprises.com — every rule below resolves
# in a single hop directly to its final destination (no redirect chains).
#
# 1. Apex + old .html paths -> final www clean URL, in one hop.
#    (Placed before the generic apex catch-all so these specific matches win first.)
https://shs-enterprises.com/index.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/ 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/about.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/about 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/services.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/services 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/contact.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/contact 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/watch.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/watch 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/portfolio.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/portfolio 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/blog.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/blog 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/blog-post.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/blog-post 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/policies.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/policies 301
https://shs-enterprises.com/policy.html https://www.shs-enterprises.com/policy 301

# 2. Everything else on the apex domain -> same path on www, in one hop.
#    Catches apex/, apex/assets/*, and any apex URL not covered above.
https://shs-enterprises.com/* https://www.shs-enterprises.com/:splat 301

# 3. On www itself, old .html paths -> their clean equivalent, in one hop.
/index.html / 301
/about.html /about 301
/services.html /services 301
/contact.html /contact 301
/watch.html /watch 301
/portfolio.html /portfolio 301
/blog.html /blog 301
/blog-post.html /blog-post 301
/policies.html /policies 301
/policy.html /policy 301
